<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The backend is plain HTTP on the ward LAN (http://<pc-ip>:8000), and Android 9+
  blocks cleartext by default. Without this the APK builds and installs fine, then
  every request fails with "CLEARTEXT communication not permitted" - which reaches
  Flutter as a generic Dio connection error and looks like a wrong IP or a dead
  server.

  Cleartext is permitted broadly rather than pinned to specific addresses on
  purpose. Android matches <domain> entries against a hostname or an exact IP and
  cannot express a subnet, so an allow-list would have to name the server's exact
  address - which is DHCP-assigned and has already moved twice. Pinning it would
  swap one silent failure for another, harder one: the app would work until the
  lease changed and then fail in a way indistinguishable from a dead backend.

  REMOVE THIS once the backend is served over TLS. It is the reason this build is
  a lab tool and not something to hand to a ward.
-->
<network-security-config>
    <base-config cleartextTrafficPermitted="true" />
</network-security-config>
